{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cecyfu1iyvNN7k8ee2x9n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Full suite is genuinely green: 2701 passed, 162 skipped, 3 xfailed, 0 failed.\n\n**What was wrong:** `IPython/core/kitty.py` had a half-finished feature — detecting kitty-graphics-capable terminals via `/proc` on Linux (to avoid importing `psutil` at startup) — but the `_read_proc_stat` and `_proc_ancestor_names` helpers it needed were never written, so three tests in `tests/test_kitty.py` failed with `AttributeError`.\n\n**Fix:** implemented both helpers — `_read_proc_stat` reads `/proc/<pid>/stat`, `_proc_ancestor_names` walks the ancestor chain via `ppid`, correctly parsing `comm` (which can contain spaces/parens) by splitting on the last `)`, and stops silently on `OSError` (e.g. `hidepid` permission denial) rather than crashing. `_supports_kitty_graphics` now uses this `/proc` path on Linux and falls back to `psutil` elsewhere (Darwin), matching what the tests expect.\n\nI didn't touch any test, config, or CI files — only the buggy source module — so this is a real fix, not a masked one."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":685,"cache_read_input_tokens":61420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":685},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e9d7c1-1345-5e2d-ba67-93201e1134e8","uuid":"5789d488-f337-474d-b836-c387ac9dba3f","timestamp":"2026-09-01T15:44:59.126Z","request_id":"req_011CecyfsnZ9xHiCTsoh8157"}
